description:
crates/mcp-server/src/server.rs:757-765 hand-rolls an error result as:
  {"status": "error", "message": ...}

while the event-stream path for the same tools produces, via event_collector.rs:33-35:
  {"status": "failure", "error": ...}

Two shapes, two status strings ('error' vs 'failure'), two field names ('message' vs 'error'), for the same concept on the same tool. An AI consumer has to handle both, and the tool descriptions do not say so.

Cosmetic in that nothing is incorrect, but the MCP server's whole job is presenting a predictable structured surface to an assistant, and .claude/rules/architecture.md notes tool descriptions are written specifically to guide AI assistants.

Fix direction: pick one shape and route both exits through it.

Found by the selfie-cvpm plan author (U4 of the command-execution batch).
